      * '\x01' (0x01) is a control character (< 0x20, not tab/newline) and should be
        classified as non-text by the program's BC_READ_BIN_CHAR predicate
      * '\n' (0x0A) terminates the line so bc_read_buf/bc_read_line complete normally

    No command-line arguments are passed, and stdin is a non-tty pipe via subprocess,
    ensuring history/TTY interfaces are not used.
